    "description": "Scientific and engineering vessel-design study combining hydrodynamics, propulsion, energy efficiency, cost analysis, and underwater radiated-noise reduction. Domestic institutions eligible; preference for US-company/US-flag team leads is evaluative, not an exclusion. An organization can join multiple teams but may lead only one proposal; no identical teams rotating leads. SAM registration/current UEI required for application and award. MARAD funds100% through cooperative agreements; generally$150k–$450k,12–18months. Vessel classes/preferences and Amendments4/5 Q&A apply: whale-watching catamarans are outside preferred vessel types, and all fishing vessels, including large commercial vessels, are outside the specific RFP focus. Eligibility basis: All domestic applicant types except individuals includes domestic universities; the proposal is for a research/design study, not acquisition of a finished vessel. Submission: PDF proposal by email to both listed MARAD acquisition contacts per SectionE.4; no separate application package required.",
